# Generated TypeScript types — do not edit (PRD §6.13, NFR-33). Emitted by
# ts-rs from the Rust types carrying `#[ts(export)]`, and committed so the
# frontend reads the contract without a Rust toolchain.
#
# Regenerate with `npm run bindings:generate`; `npm run bindings:check` (which
# `pretypecheck` runs) fails if what is committed here is not what the Rust
# types produce right now.
#
# Not `models/` yet, despite what this file said while the directory was empty:
# `models/` holds no types at all so far, and the one file here comes from
# `db::Migration` — see the comment above that struct for why the generator is
# proven on it and why that is not the beginning of the Appendix D catalogue.
